From ddfdb53f76b5ec32d2e4fbc9ad92ea27cab57e99 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: "vincent.yen" <vincent.yen@mitaccomputing.com>
Date: Tue, 22 Sep 2026 09:02:38 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] cpld: improve firmware update safety and diagnostics

Add Redfish events for firmware update start, completion, and failure.
Return proper D-Bus errors for concurrent updates and unsupported apply
times. Propagate detailed Lattice update failure stages through temporary
error logs and remove the logs after they are consumed.

Resolve dynamic I2C buses from Entity Manager MuxChannel configuration
when Bus is unavailable. Require a successful CPLD version read before
publishing software objects in production builds, and derive each
Software.Version.Purpose from its configured CPLD chip name.

Add a process-wide CPLD reboot guard using dedicated systemd drop-ins for
reboot, poweroff, and halt targets. Reference count concurrent updates,
clean up stale guards at startup, and track inactive, active, and unknown
states. Retry guard removal three times and preserve a safe state when
cleanup fails.

Ensure the reboot guard is released when the vendor update returns or
throws. Also provide a CPLD_DEBUG mode that simulates a 60-second update
without programming the device.

Upstream-Status: Inappropriate [No upstream maintenance]
